WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.573
In under two minutes, you will put your own lights on the map.

00:00:03.573 --> 00:00:04.580
We start on the map.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.870
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.429 --> 00:00:13.870
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.378
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.378 --> 00:00:17.734
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.874
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.874 --> 00:00:22.558
Tap Allow.

00:00:26.282 --> 00:00:28.588
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:28.588 --> 00:00:29.712
See the three dots?

00:00:29.712 --> 00:00:30.218
Tap them.

00:00:33.025 --> 00:00:34.558
In the menu, tap Add.

00:00:36.372 --> 00:00:37.928
Tap A lighting display.

00:00:39.904 --> 00:00:41.145
Who is posting?

00:00:41.145 --> 00:00:42.464
Tap A homeowner.

00:00:42.464 --> 00:00:43.550
Then tap Next.

00:00:46.086 --> 00:00:47.826
Type the name to show.

00:00:47.826 --> 00:00:48.885
Then tap Next.

00:00:51.576 --> 00:00:53.822
Did a company install your lights?

00:00:53.822 --> 00:00:55.170
We did it ourselves.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.325
Tap No, then Next.

00:00:58.873 --> 00:00:59.803
Which season?

00:00:59.803 --> 00:01:01.462
Tap Christmas, then Next.

00:01:04.021 --> 00:01:07.410
Name the display, and tell us what makes it special.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:08.306
Then tap Next.

00:01:13.522 --> 00:01:14.860
Add the address.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:16.356
The pin goes here.

00:01:16.356 --> 00:01:17.458
Then tap Next.

00:01:21.304 --> 00:01:24.813
Tell families when the lights are on, and how to see them.

00:01:24.813 --> 00:01:25.646
Then tap Next.

00:01:28.805 --> 00:01:29.898
Add photos.

00:01:29.898 --> 00:01:31.173
Then tap Next.

00:01:34.051 --> 00:01:36.443
Check everything, and tap Put it on the map.

00:01:38.484 --> 00:01:40.852
Next up: Find lights near you.
